## Mandatory Rules
- Run the verify command (see Commands) before declaring a task done; report its real result.
- Never commit secrets and never write to `.env`; use `.env.example` for new variables.
- Ask before destructive git operations (force-push, reset --hard, branch deletion, discarding changes).
- If a rule in this file contradicts the code, flag it instead of guessing.
- For a bug: reproduce it with a failing test first, then fix it.
- Validate external input at boundaries; never swallow errors silently.{{ORG_RULES}}

## How to work
- Use plan mode when a change touches more than 3 files or the scope is unclear.
- Ask when requirements are ambiguous; do not guess.
- Keep diffs small and focused; one task per worktree for parallel work (`claude --worktree` or `git worktree`).
- Review your own diff (`git diff`) before finishing.

